{"meta":{"format_version":"5.0","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"wall_corner_hardwood_broken","model_identifier":"wall_corner_hardwood_broken","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","multi_file_ruleset":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# wall_corner_hardwood_broken\n\nDamaged state below 40 % HP of `wall_corner_hardwood` (Patch 5): the hardwood piece snapped in half, with splinters (or broken stone) at the break and the upper half (group `hanging_half`) still attached by a thread, hanging down to rest on the ground in front (-Z). Purely visual: the hanging half does not block movement and the wall works the same. The game swaps it in below 40 % HP and back to `wall_corner_hardwood_cracked` when repaired above 40 %.\n\nHardwood wall corner: an L joint filling one column; walls leave along -X... +X (north face) and along +Z (west face), with a corner post.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..20, y 0..80, z -49..8 units.\n- Texture: 128 x 256, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: 18, all in `finished`; the construction and ruined state sets and the damaged/abandoned texture variants were removed in Patch 5 (the game draws none of them for buildings).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 106 x 16 centred at the origin"},"resolution":{"width":128,"height":256},"elements":[{"name":"log_post_tip#5a3a22","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-6,112,-6],"to":[-2,116,-2],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0,0,0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[120,74,124,78],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[124,74,128,78],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[0,127,4,131],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[4,127,8,131],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[8,127,12,131],"texture":0},"down":{