ront (-Z). Purely visual: the hanging half does not block movement and the wall works the same. The game swaps it in below 40 % HP and back to `wall_corner_hardwood_cracked` when repaired above 40 %.\n\nHardwood wall corner: an L joint filling one column; walls leave along -X... +X (north face) and along +Z (west face), with a corner post.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..20, y 0..80, z -49..8 units.\n- Texture: 128 x 256, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: 18, all in `finished`; the construction and ruined state sets and the damaged/abandoned texture variants were removed in Patch 5 (the game draws none of them for buildings).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 106 x 16 centred at the origin"}